# Build context is motion/. The image COPYs exactly two things — app/ and
# docker/package.json — so everything below is either dead weight in the context
# or a local artifact that would bust the app layer's cache on every render.
#
# NOTE: docker only reads an ignore file at the CONTEXT root (motion/.dockerignore)
# or named after the Dockerfile (motion/docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore). It does
# NOT read motion/docker/.dockerignore. build_and_push.sh copies this file to the
# name docker actually reads before every build, so the two cannot drift.

# CDK app: node_modules and cdk.out here run to hundreds of MB and never ship.
cdk/

# Local iteration leftovers. common.py puts its scratch in SERVE_ROOT/work/<id>,
# which is motion/work/ when the tools are run from a checkout instead of the
# image — frames, wavs and mp4s by the gigabyte.
work/
app/out/
app/probe/
app/frames/

# Never a build input: every wav and mp4 in this tree is render output. Note the
# absence of a `data/` rule — the pieces fetch `data/<name>.json` relative to the
# page, so that directory name has to stay copyable.
**/*.wav
**/*.mp4

**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.DS_Store

# Not needed inside the image.
CONTRACT.md
docker/build_and_push.sh
docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore

.git
.gitignore
*.log
